<rss version="2.0"><channel><title>Brickset</title><link>https://brickset.com</link><description>LEGO news from Brickset</description><copyright>Copyright (C) 1997-2026, Brickset ltd.</copyright><generator>Brickset RSS Generator</generator><item><title>Vintage set of the week: Small basic set</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136135</link><author>Huwbot</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136135</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/sets/small/1-12.jpg' alt="Vintage set of the week: Small basic set"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;This week's vintage set is &lt;a href='/sets/1-12'&gt;1&lt;/a&gt; Small basic set, released during 1977. It's one of &lt;a href='/sets/theme-Minitalia/year-1977'&gt;2 Minitalia sets&lt;/a&gt; produced that year. It contains &lt;a href='/inventories/1-12/rebrickable'&gt;91 pieces&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It's owned by 38 Brickset members. If you want to add it to your collection you might find it for sale at &lt;a href='https://www.brickowl.com/search/catalog?query=1-12&amp;jump=1&amp;cat=3&amp;utm_source=brickset'&gt;Brick Owl&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href='https://bricklink.com/v2/catalog/catalogitem.page?S=1-12#T=S'&gt;BrickLink&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href='/buy/ebay/?query=1-12'&gt;eBay&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136135/vintage-set-of-the-week-small-basic-set"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:01:02 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Best modular building: Quarter final results</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136125</link><author>Huw</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136125</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/135935_mbc.jpg' alt="Best modular building: Quarter final results"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;Over 11,000 votes were cast during the quarter-final bouts in our quest to crown the best modular building.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The results are in, and can be viewed after the break.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136125/best-modular-building-quarter-final-results"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Review: 75459 Imperial Lambda-class Shuttle</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/132384</link><author>CapnRex101</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/132384</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/132384_Lambda 1.jpg' alt="Review: 75459 Imperial Lambda-class Shuttle"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;There have been &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/tag-Lambda-Class-T-4A-Imperial-Shuttle"&gt;many versions&lt;/a&gt; of the famous Lambda-class shuttle produced over the past 25 years, of which &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/75094-1/Imperial-Shuttle-Tydirium"&gt;75094&lt;/a&gt; Imperial Shuttle Tydirium is usually considered the best play set. However, the new design could challenge the model from 2015, given its sleek bodywork.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/75459-1/Imperial-Lambda-class-Shuttle"&gt;75459&lt;/a&gt; Imperial Lambda-class Shuttle includes a couple of great minifigures as well. Moff Gideon and Dr. Pershing are particularly appealing, although only having five characters in a set that costs &amp;pound;139.99, $139.99 or &amp;euro;149.99 is underwhelming. Even so, this could be the best Imperial Shuttle play set to date.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/132384/review-75459-imperial-lambda-class-shuttle"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Random set of the day: Ogel Control Centre</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136121</link><author>Huwbot</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136121</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/sets/small/6776-1.jpg' alt="Random set of the day: Ogel Control Centre"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today's random set is &lt;a href='/sets/6776-1'&gt;6776&lt;/a&gt; Ogel Control Centre, released during 2001. It's one of &lt;a href='/sets/theme-Alpha-Team/year-2001'&gt;6 Alpha Team sets&lt;/a&gt; produced that year. It contains &lt;a href='/inventories/6776-1'&gt;411 pieces&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href='/minifigs/in-6776-1'&gt;3 minifigs&lt;/a&gt;, and its retail price was US$49.99, which equates to about US$91 in today's money.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It's owned by 1,389 Brickset members. If you want to add it to your collection you should find it for sale at &lt;a href='https://www.brickowl.com/search/catalog?query=6776-1&amp;jump=1&amp;cat=3&amp;utm_source=brickset'&gt;Brick Owl&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href='https://www.bricklink.com/v2/catalog/catalogitem.page?S=6776-1#T=S'&gt;BrickLink&lt;/a&gt;, where new ones sell for around $248.00,  or &lt;a href='/buy/ebay/?query=6776-1'&gt;eBay&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136121/random-set-of-the-day-ogel-control-centre"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:01:02 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>BrickLink back online</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136115</link><author>CapnRex101</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136115</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/136115_Screenshot 2026-11-12 204424.png' alt="BrickLink back online"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;A week after &lt;a href="https://www.bricklink.com/v2/main.page"&gt;BrickLink&lt;/a&gt; was taken offline, the website is back and a more detailed statement has been issued, confirming that some BrickLink members&amp;#39; usernames and IP addresses were accessed, along with a &amp;#39;very small number&amp;#39; of email addresses, but no passwords or financial information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Affected members will apparently be contacted and &lt;a href="https://www.bricklink.com/help.asp?helpID=2720"&gt;the full statement&lt;/a&gt; is available to read on BrickLink.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Minifigure images have thus returned to the Brickset database and everything on BrickLink seems to be working again too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:55:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>2027 LEGO Star Wars sets announced!</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136103</link><author>CapnRex101</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136103</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/136103_75467_Prod_pSD5PBktl6Ea.jpg' alt="2027 LEGO Star Wars sets announced!"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;Seven new Star Wars sets have been announced, the first of many celebrating the 50th anniversary of Star Wars in 2027!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These include four play sets, each containing a minifigure based on Ralph McQuarrie&amp;#39;s concept art for characters in the original movie, as well as three 18+ sets, which come with printed 6x8 poster tiles. The sets announced today will be released on January 1st.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Highlights for me include the 3209-piece &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/75467-1/A-New-Hope-Movie-Poster"&gt;75467&lt;/a&gt; A New Hope Movie Poster, which I think looks amazing, plus &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/75470-1/Mustafar-Duel"&gt;75470&lt;/a&gt; Mustafar Duel and &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/75478-1/Rebel-Y-wing-Starfighter"&gt;75478&lt;/a&gt; Rebel Y-wing Starfighter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;View all seven sets and their prices after the break...&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136103/2027-lego-star-wars-sets-announced!"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:15:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Random set of the day: Construction Workers</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136093</link><author>Huwbot</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136093</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/sets/small/6628-2.jpg' alt="Random set of the day: Construction Workers"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today's random set is &lt;a href='/sets/6628-2'&gt;6628&lt;/a&gt; Construction Workers, released during 1984. It's one of &lt;a href='/sets/theme-Town/year-1984'&gt;17 Town sets&lt;/a&gt; produced that year. It contains &lt;a href='/inventories/6628-2'&gt;20 pieces&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href='/minifigs/in-6628-2'&gt;4 minifigs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It's owned by 96 Brickset members. If you want to add it to your collection you should find it for sale at &lt;a href='https://www.brickowl.com/search/catalog?query=6628-2&amp;jump=1&amp;cat=3&amp;utm_source=brickset'&gt;Brick Owl&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href='https://www.bricklink.com/v2/catalog/catalogitem.page?S=6628-2#T=S'&gt;BrickLink&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href='/buy/ebay/?query=6628-2'&gt;eBay&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136093/random-set-of-the-day-construction-workers"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:01:03 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Best modular building: Quarter final bout 4</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136041</link><author>Huw</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136041</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/136041_bout3.jpg' alt="Best modular building: Quarter final bout 4"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&amp;#39;ve come to the last bout of the quarter finals in our quest to crown your favourite modular building already!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This one sees &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/10251-1"&gt;10251&lt;/a&gt; Brick Bank advocated for by &lt;em&gt;RichardGoring &lt;/em&gt;battle &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/10255-1"&gt;10255&lt;/a&gt; Assembly Square championed by &lt;em&gt;MeganL&lt;/em&gt; for the last place in the semi-finals.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Read their pitches after the break then cast your vote for your favourite. I&amp;#39;ll reveal the results on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136041/best-modular-building-quarter-final-bout-4"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:30:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>BrickLink issues statement on downtime</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136081</link><author>CapnRex101</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136081</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/136081_BrickLink 1.jpg' alt="BrickLink issues statement on downtime"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;BrickLink has now been offline for almost a week and a few minutes before it was estimated to be back online, at 18:00 CET today, &lt;a href="https://maintenance.bricklink.com/recovery.html"&gt;the website&lt;/a&gt; has been updated with a brief comment regarding its status, which follows:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;#39;We took BrickLink offline after identifying unusual activity on the platform. Our immediate priority was to secure the site, protect our members and ensure the integrity of BrickLink.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Before bringing the site back online, we need to fully understand what has happened. That means containing the issue, investigating how it happened and checking for related issues.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;This work is still on-going and we appreciate your patience while we work to get things back online as soon as possible.&amp;#39;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The statement is pretty vague and I cannot speculate on possible reasons for this issue, but the comment that they are still trying to understand what happened does not exactly fill me with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nonetheless, hopefully the issue is resolved soon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:05:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Two 2027 LEGO Fortnite sets revealed!</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136077</link><author>CapnRex101</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136077</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/136077_Banana 4.jpg' alt="Two 2027 LEGO Fortnite sets revealed!"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two new LEGO Fortnite sets have been announced, ahead of their release on January 1st.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/77084-1/P-1000"&gt;77084&lt;/a&gt; P-1000 is definitely the more eye-catching of the pair for me, capturing the unique limb design of the &amp;#39;banandroid&amp;#39; from the game! I am sure this model will look great alongside &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/77072-1/Peely-Bone"&gt;77072&lt;/a&gt; Peely Bone and &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/77081-1/KIT"&gt;77081&lt;/a&gt; KIT. The minifigure included is excellent too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/77088-1/Guaco-s-Tacos"&gt;77088&lt;/a&gt; Guaco&amp;#39;s Tacos has been unveiled too. Neither set is listed on LEGO.com currently, so their prices have yet to be confirmed for all regions, but the P-1000 will cost &amp;euro;89.99 and Guaco&amp;#39;s Tacos is expected to cost &amp;euro;19.99.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;View both sets below...&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136077/two-2027-lego-fortnite-sets-revealed!"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:30:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Best modular building: Quarter final bout 3</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136043</link><author>Huw</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136043</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/136043_bout4.jpg' alt="Best modular building: Quarter final bout 3"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;We continue our quest to crown the best modular building today with two more quarter-final bouts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two olive green buildings face up to each other in this one: &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/10243-1"&gt;10243&lt;/a&gt; Parisian Restaurant advocated for by &lt;em&gt;rljf311, and &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/10326-1"&gt;10326&lt;/a&gt; Natural History Museum, by Matt89190&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Which one will get your vote?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136043/best-modular-building-quarter-final-bout-3"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Random set of the day: Power Pitstop</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136065</link><author>Huwbot</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136065</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/sets/small/6467-1.jpg' alt="Random set of the day: Power Pitstop"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today's random set is &lt;a href='/sets/6467-1'&gt;6467&lt;/a&gt; Power Pitstop, released during 1999. It's one of &lt;a href='/sets/theme-Town/year-1999'&gt;63 Town sets&lt;/a&gt; produced that year. It contains &lt;a href='/inventories/6467-1'&gt;66 pieces&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href='/minifigs/in-6467-1'&gt;2 minifigs&lt;/a&gt;, and its retail price was US$10, which equates to about US$19 in today's money.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It's owned by 1,336 Brickset members. If you want to add it to your collection you should find it for sale at &lt;a href='https://www.brickowl.com/search/catalog?query=6467-1&amp;jump=1&amp;cat=3&amp;utm_source=brickset'&gt;Brick Owl&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href='https://www.bricklink.com/v2/catalog/catalogitem.page?S=6467-1#T=S'&gt;BrickLink&lt;/a&gt;, where new ones sell for around $35.00,  or &lt;a href='/buy/ebay/?query=6467-1'&gt;eBay&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136065/random-set-of-the-day-power-pitstop"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:01:02 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Best modular building: Quarter final bout 2</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136039</link><author>Huw</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136039</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/136039_bout2.jpg' alt="Best modular building: Quarter final bout 2"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;The second of four quarter-final bouts in our quest to find your favourite modular building sees two of my favourites go head-to head: &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/10297-1"&gt;10297&lt;/a&gt; Boutique Hotel and &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/10350-1"&gt;10350&lt;/a&gt; Tudor Corner&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Read what &lt;em&gt;Bluey2000 &lt;/em&gt;and &lt;em&gt;ToaDraconis &lt;/em&gt;have to say about them after the break, then cast your vote for your favourite.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136039/best-modular-building-quarter-final-bout-2"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Best modular building: Quarter final bout 1</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136037</link><author>Huw</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136037</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/136037_bout1.jpg' alt="Best modular building: Quarter final bout 1"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is the first bout in the knockout phase of our quest to find your favourite modular building which sees &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/10246-1"&gt;10246&lt;/a&gt; Detective&amp;#39;s Office take on &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/sets/10260-1"&gt;10260&lt;/a&gt; Downtown Diner, advocated for by &lt;em&gt;AustinPowers &lt;/em&gt;and &lt;em&gt;ForestMenOfEndor &lt;/em&gt;respectively.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Read what they have to say about them after the break, then cast your vote for the one you&amp;#39;ve been persuaded is the best of the two.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136037/best-modular-building-quarter-final-bout-1"&gt;Continue reading »&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;copy; 2026 &lt;a href='https://brickset.com/'&gt;Brickset.com&lt;/a&gt;. Republication prohibited without prior permission.&lt;em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:00:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>LEGO Ideas backlog</title><link>https://brickset.com/article/136018</link><author>Huw</author><guid>https://brickset.com/article/136018</guid><description>&lt;img style='float:left; margin: 0 10px 10px 0; max-width: 240px; max-height: 240px;' src='https://images.brickset.com/news/thumbs/large/136018_smurfs.jpg' alt="LEGO Ideas backlog"/&gt;&lt;p&gt;Following the &lt;a href="https://brickset.com/article/136017/first-2026-ideas-review-period-results-announced"&gt;announcement of the first 2026 review period results&lt;/a&gt; yesterday, here is the updated list of the projects that have been approved but have not yet made it onto the shelves.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Passed review&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;table class="neattable"&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
		&lt;tr&gt;
